public static List<ThreadSnapshot> parseFromFileWithTimeRange(File file, List<ProfileAnalyzeTimeRange> timeRanges) throws IOException {
    // Load thread snapshots from file
    List<ThreadSnapshot> snapshots = new ArrayList<>();
    try (BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(file))) {
        String line;
        while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
            // Parse line format
            String[] tokens = line.trim().split("\\s+");
            if (tokens.length < 3) {
                continue;
            }
            long timestamp = Long.parseLong(tokens[0]);
            String threadId = tokens[1];
            String threadName = tokens[2];
            ThreadSnapshot snapshot = new ThreadSnapshot(threadId, threadName, timestamp);
            snapshots.add(snapshot);
        }
    }

    // Filter snapshots by time range
    List<ThreadSnapshot> filteredSnapshots = new ArrayList<>();
    for (ThreadSnapshot snapshot : snapshots) {
        for (ProfileAnalyzeTimeRange range : timeRanges) {
            if (snapshot.getTimestamp() >= range.getFrom() && snapshot.getTimestamp() <= range.getTo()) {
                filteredSnapshots.add(snapshot);
                break;
            }
        }
    }
    return filteredSnapshots;
}
```
This method takes a file and a list of time ranges as input, and reads the contents of the file line by line. It then parses each line and extracts the thread ID, name, and timestamp, and converts them into a `ThreadSnapshot` object.

The method then filters the snapshots by the time range, keeping only those that fall within the specified time range. Finally, it returns the filtered list of `ThreadSnapshot` objects.
